Can you please send at least the function getPopVec?  If only putting that in the model causes the compilation failure, that might not be compiling.

You can test compilation of that outside of the model, i.e.

CgetPopVec <- compileNimble(getPopVec)

and debug from there in the simpler context.

There shouldn't be a problem with whatever R function you happen to call from an R function that is called via a nimbleRcall.

If you send the whole function or the whole example I will take a look.

Perry

